  - line: 83
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 2: THE WELCOME PARTY - PROTOCOL OF ABSENCE"
  - line: 85
    type: narration
    text: "Walking between the shadow entities was an exercise in existential discomfort."
  - line: 86
    type: narration
    text: "They had no faces, no discernible features, yet Geralt felt the weight of their attention—not as eyes, but as a subtle cooling of the air around him, a slight increase in resistance, as if reality itself was examining them."
  - line: 88
    type: narration
    text: "The applicator in his head had given up entirely, displaying only: < ENVIRONMENT: NON-PARSABLE."
  - line: 89
    type: narration
    text: "THREAT ASSESSMENT: INDETERMINATE. >"
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "The dragon armor remained tense, plates shifting minutely, as if trying to align against a threat with no vector."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "After what felt like miles of silent marching, the corridor opened into a vast courtyard before the Spire itself."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "The structure was architecture turned inside out—buttresses that defied gravity, arches that led into solid walls, stairways that spiraled into their own beginnings."
  - line: 95
    type: narration
    text: "It was carved from crystallized shadow, drinking what little luminescence they carried."
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "At the base of the grand entrance stood a single figure."
  - line: 98
    type: narration
    text: "Tall, robed in darkness that seemed to drift like smoke."
  - line: 99
    type: narration
    text: "Where a face should be was a smooth, featureless plane that reflected nothing."
  - line: 101
    type: narration
    text: "Its voice was not sound, but vibration—windchimes made of bone, heard in the marrow."
  - line: 103
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The Anchor arrives. Luminaire's vessel. You are expected.\""
  - line: 105
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"Are you the Keeper?\""
  - line: 107
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I am the Herald. The Umbra Sovereign will see you now.\""
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "It turned, robe flowing like liquid night. \"But understand: you are not here to reclaim property. You are here to negotiate your survival. The terms have changed.\""
  - line: 110
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"

